# A file at the code-spill path this compile did not write must not reach its C
# (issues/fixed/2026-10-23-concurrent-compiles-of-one-output-share-the-code-spill-file.md).
#
# The compile used to decide whether to splice `<output>.yo-code-spill` into
# the C by whether that path existed, and two compiles of one output shared the
# path. On 2026-10-22 and 2026-10-23 a `yo build` re-run beside the orphaned
# compile child of a killed one lost its spill: the other compile finished
# first and deleted the file, so the C went out without the runtime and every
# spilled function body, and clang failed on `__yo_borrow_assert_unborrowed`.
#
# The fixture plants a foreign spill at the old shared path. This program is
# far too small to spill (the threshold is 8 MiB of function bodies), so a
# compile that decides by its own spilled byte count ignores the file and
# leaves it alone. The pre-fix compile spliced it into `app.c`, the C compiler
# hit the planted `#error`, and the file was deleted.
stdout_keep=^(Using |error|.*#error)
timeout=300
